# Third-party licenses

The Notch has one third-party code dependency, Sparkle, and bundles one third-party font. Both are
listed below.

## Included

### Sparkle

- **Version:** 2.10.0 (`from: 2.10.0`, resolved by Swift Package Manager)
- **Copyright:** Copyright (c) 2006-2013 Andy Matuschak, and the other contributors listed in its
  licence text
- **License:** MIT, with bundled components under their own permissive licences (bsdiff, BSD-2-Clause;
  sais-lite, MIT; Ed25519, Zlib)
- **Source:** https://github.com/sparkle-project/Sparkle
- **Linked at:** the `Sparkle` Swift package, into `Contents/Frameworks/Sparkle.framework`
- **Modifications:** none
- **Licence text:** `The Notch/Resources/Licenses/Sparkle-LICENSE.txt`, copied into the app bundle
  at build time

### Departure Mono

- **Version:** 1.500
- **Copyright:** Copyright 2022–2024 Helena Zhang (helenazhang.com)
- **License:** SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
- **Source:** https://github.com/rektdeckard/departure-mono
- **Bundled at:** `The Notch/Resources/Fonts/DepartureMono-Regular.otf`
- **Modifications:** none — the released OTF is shipped verbatim.

The full OFL text ships alongside the font at
`The Notch/Resources/Fonts/DepartureMono-LICENSE.txt`.

The OFL permits bundling and redistributing the font inside a larger work under any licence,
including this MIT project. It must not be sold on its own, and a Reserved Font Name must not be
reused on a modified version; the font is shipped unmodified. The OFL text ships with the app.

